# Nothing here is COPYed by api/seed/pipeline.Dockerfile -- they take
# pyproject.toml, uv.lock, src, alembic and nothing else. This file is about the
# build CONTEXT, which is uploaded to the daemon in full before any COPY runs.
#
# A local .venv holding pvlib, pandas, scipy and friends is most of a gigabyte,
# and paying that upload on every `docker compose up` is the difference between
# a build that looks broken and one that looks fast.
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.hypothesis
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache

# Offline-plane inputs: large, regenerable, and some of it is licensed imagery
# that must not be redistributed (same rule as .gitignore).
data
*.tif
*.tiff
*.mbtiles
checkpoints
*.pt
*.pth

.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
